# Desk

Student deadline desk. No login. No database. One JSON file.

## Layout

- `backend/` is FastAPI. Run it with `uvicorn main:app --app-dir backend --port 8741`.
- `backend/ical_parser.py` is the iCal parser. Extend call sites around it. Do not rewrite `parse_ical`, the type rules, or the shipped examples.
- `frontend/` is Next.js. It proxies `/api/*` to the backend.
- `data/state.json` is the only persistence. It is created on first run and is gitignored.
- `data/sample-calendar.ics` is the demo feed behind "Load sample calendar".
- `data/state.example.json` shows the empty document shape.

## Model

Stored in `data/state.json`:

- `profile`: waking hours (`wake`, `sleep` as HH:MM on the same day), `fixed_commitments` (id, title, course, day, start, end), `preferred_study_windows` (day, start, end), `daily_capacity_hours`.
- `items`: id, title, course, type (`assignment`, `quiz`, `exam`, `event`, `personal`), `due_or_start`, source (`canvas`, `voice`, `manual`), `estimated_effort_hours`, `locked`, status (`open`, `done`), plus `description` carried from the feed.
- `plans`: `week_start` (Monday), `blocks`, `version`, `previous_version`, `change_log`.
- `undo_stack`: snapshots of profile, items, and plans from before each planner change. The stack itself is not part of a snapshot.
- A block has id, `item_id` (the linked item, or null), start, end, kind (`study`, `fixed`, `personal`, `buffer`), status (`scheduled`, `done`, `skipped`), reason.

Versions are per week. Posting a plan appends a new version and points `previous_version` at the previous one.

## Rules

- Time zone is America/Los_Angeles. Weeks start Monday. A naive datetime from the form is Pacific wall time.
- Exam and midterm titles classify as `exam` and are locked. Re-import keeps effort and status for an existing id.
- Feed imports use source `canvas`. Typed deadlines use source `manual`. `voice` is a stored source with no capture UI yet.
- Do not add login, accounts, or a database.
- Keep the frontend on shadcn/ui primitives already in `frontend/src/components/ui`.

## Planning

Gemini planning lives in `backend/planning/`. `POST /api/plan/gemini` reads `GEMINI_API_KEY`. `GEMINI_MODEL` is optional and defaults to `gemini-2.5-flash`.

Tools: `list_items`, `add_item`, `move_item`, `create_blocks`, `move_block`, `delete_block`, `get_week_plan`, `set_constraint`, `mark_progress`, `undo_last_change`.

The validator rejects overlaps, blocks outside waking hours, study and personal time over daily capacity, and any move of a locked deadline. Invalid plans are retried once. Do not regenerate imported deadlines. Do not modify the voice loop.
